// `file_write_binary` reports status too, and its declaration was wrong in the
// same way as `file_write`'s: the checker said TY_VOID while the runtime
// returned a count.
//
// Success returns the number of bytes written, which is the array's length —
// not 0, and not a boolean. A failure returns -1. Both are checked here because
// the two return values are what a caller has to be able to tell apart.
//
// Expected: 3
// Expected: -1
fn main() {
    println(file_write_binary([65, 66, 67], "/tmp/ionic_io_probe_binary.bin"));
    // Same directory-missing failure as write_fail.ionic, so the two write
    // builtins are shown to agree about what "failed" means.
    println(file_write_binary([65], "/tmp/ionic_io_probe_no_such_dir/y.bin"));
}
